.TH SDL_vasprintf 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_vasprintf \- This works exactly like vasprintf() but doesn\(aqt require access to a C runtime.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "int SDL_vasprintf(char **strp, const char *fmt, va_list ap);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Functions identically to
.BR SDL_asprintf (),
except it takes a
.BR va_list
instead of using
.BR \[char46]\[char46]\[char46]
variable arguments\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I strp
on output, is set to the new string\[char46] Must not be NULL\[char46]
.TP
.I fmt
a printf-style format string\[char46] Must not be NULL\[char46]
.TP
.I ap
a
.BR va_list
values to be used with the format string\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of bytes in the newly-allocated string, not counting the null-terminator char, or a negative value on error\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

